<title>USA: Magnum Hunter completes acquisition.</title>
<headline>Magnum Hunter completes acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>IRVING, Texas 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Magnum Hunter Resources Inc said it has closed on the purchase of about 1,900 oil and natural gas wells in 25 field areas in West Texas and 21 field areas in Southeast New Mexico containing over 3,100 oil and gas completions.</p>
<p>Magnum Hunter said it paid Burlington Resources Inc about $133 million for these Permian Basin properties which are now producing abpit 26.7 million cubic feet of natural gas and 2,500 barrels of oil daily.</p>
<p>The company said it estimates the monthly cash flow from these properties to be about $2.2 million.</p>
<p>Magnum Hunter said it estimates to properties contained proved reserves of 15.3 million barrels of oil and 99.9 billion cubic feet of natural gas for a total of 191.6 billion cubic feet a day gas equivalents on January 1.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
